  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AU-C 505.A15, the primary risk of electronic confirmations is the inability to adequately verify the identity and authority of the respondent. Unlike paper confirmations sent to verified physical addresses, electronic responses may be intercepted, altered, or submitted by unauthorized individuals, undermining evidence reliability.
Wrong (A): Electronic confirmations are not inherently less reliable than paper — reliability depends on controls over the confirmation process, not the delivery method.
