-- Q1314: Ethics and Independence [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the AICPA Code of Professional Conduct (ET 1.240), an immaterial indirect financial interest — such as owning shares in a diversified mutual fund that holds client stock — does not impair independence. The interest is indirect because it is not directly controlled, and immaterial to the covered member.
Wrong (A): Under ET 1.240.02, any direct financial interest in an audit client impairs independence regardless of amount — even a single directly owned share.
Wrong (B): A material indirect financial interest impairs independence because its magnitude creates a self-interest threat.
Wrong (C): A direct financial interest held in a blind trust still impairs independence — the trust structure does not change the direct nature of the interest.$EXPL$
