-- Q1333: Ethics and Independence [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the AICPA Code of Professional Conduct (ET 1.277), a former employment relationship impairs independence when the individual held a key position such as CFO, the departure was recent (one year ago), and ongoing financial ties like unvested stock options remain. These conditions create self-interest and familiarity threats that cannot be adequately mitigated.
Wrong (A): A former sales representative role three years ago with no financial ties poses minimal threat — the position lacked influence over financial reporting.
Wrong (B): A mid-level accounting position five years ago with no remaining financial connections generally would not impair independence given the elapsed time and role level.
Wrong (C): An entry-level position ten years ago poses the least threat due to the low-influence role and significant time elapsed.$EXPL$
