UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under the AICPA Code of Professional Conduct (ET 1.130), due care requires CPAs to observe the profession''s technical and ethical standards, continuously improve competence, and discharge professional responsibilities to the best of their ability. This applies regardless of industry familiarity.
Wrong (A): Due care does not require reporting every immaterial error to the audit committee — materiality thresholds guide reporting obligations.
Wrong (B): Due care does not impose arbitrary experience thresholds; CPAs may accept engagements in unfamiliar industries if they can achieve competence.
