-- Q1351: Professional Responsibilities [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AU-C 210.13, when the client authorizes communication between auditors, the predecessor should respond promptly and fully to reasonable inquiries. This includes information about management integrity, disagreements on accounting matters, fraud or illegal acts, and reasons for the auditor change.
Wrong (A): The predecessor is not required to provide unrestricted access to all workpapers — only to respond to specific, reasonable inquiries from the successor.
Wrong (C): The predecessor cannot refuse to communicate once proper client authorization has been obtained — professional standards require a response.
Wrong (D): Limiting the response to only the audit opinion would be inadequate — the successor needs information about management integrity and disagreements.$EXPL$
