  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AR-C 70.05 and the AICPA Code (ET 1.310), when a CPA prepares financial statements without performing an audit or review, a disclaimer must be included on each page stating the statements have not been audited or reviewed and no assurance is expressed. This prevents third parties from assuming verification occurred.
Wrong (B): A qualified opinion is issued during an audit engagement, not a preparation engagement — the CPA has not performed audit procedures.
