  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the AICPA Code of Professional Conduct (ET 1.110.010), when a married couple begins divorce proceedings and each spouse requests separate representation, a conflict of interest arises because their tax interests become adverse. The CPA should withdraw from representing both spouses when the conflict cannot be adequately mitigated.
