  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AR-C 90 (SSARS), significant litigation does not automatically preclude a review engagement. The CPA should evaluate whether sufficient information can be obtained through inquiry and analytical procedures to address the litigation, and whether management will make appropriate going-concern disclosures.
Wrong (B): Withdrawal is not automatically required — the CPA should first evaluate whether the review can be completed with adequate information and disclosures.
